 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "A sparrow and a crow once agreed to have *khichrî* for dinner."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "So the Sparrow brought rice, and the Crow brought lentils, and the Sparrow was cook, and when the *khichrî* was ready, the Crow stood by to claim his share."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p002.s01",
     "source": "'Who ever heard of any one sitting down to dinner so dirty as you are?' quoth the Sparrow scornfully."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s02",
     "source": "'Your body is quite black, and your head looks as if it were covered with ashes."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s03",
     "source": "For goodness gracious sake, go and wash in the Pond first.'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p002"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p003.s01",
     "source": "The Crow, though a little huffy at being called dirty, deemed it best to comply, for he knew what a determined little person the Sparrow was; so he went to the Pond, and said--"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p003"
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p004.s01",
     "source": "'Your name, sir, is Pond,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s02",
     "source": "But my name is Crow."
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s03",
     "source": "Please give me some water,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s04",
     "source": "For if you do so"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s05",
     "source": "I can wash beak and feet"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s06",
     "source": "And the nice *khichrî* eat;"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s07",
     "source": "Though I really don't know"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s08",
     "source": "What the Sparrow can mean,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s09",
     "source": "For I'm sure, as Crows go,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s10",
     "source": "I'm remarkably clean!'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p004"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p005.s01",
     "source": "But the Pond said, 'Certainly I will give you water; but first you must go to the Deer, and beg him to lend you a horn."
    },
    {
     "id": "p005.s02",
     "source": "Then with it you can dig a nice little rill for the water to flow in clean and fresh.'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p005"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p006.s01",
     "source": "So the Crow flew to the Deer, and said--"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p006"
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p007.s01",
     "source": "'Your name, sir, is Deer,"
