   ],
   "id": "p007"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p008.s01",
     "source": "But the Deer said, 'Certainly I will give you a horn; but first you must go to the Cow, and ask her to give you some milk for me to drink."
    },
    {
     "id": "p008.s02",
     "source": "Then I shall grow fat, and not mind the pain of breaking my horn.'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p008"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p009.s01",
     "source": "So the Crow flew off to the Cow, and said--"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p009"
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p010.s01",
     "source": "'Your name, ma'am, is Cow,"
