   ],
   "id": "p013"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p014.s01",
     "source": "But the Grass said, 'Certainly I will give you Grass; but first you must go to the Blacksmith, and ask him to make you a sickle."
    },
    {
     "id": "p014.s02",
     "source": "Then you can cut me, for who ever heard of Grass cutting itself?'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p014"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p015.s01",
     "source": "So the Crow went to the Blacksmith, and said--"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p015"
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p016.s01",
     "source": "'Your name, sir, is Smith,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s02",
     "source": "But my name is Crow."
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s03",
     "source": "Please give me a sickle,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s04",
     "source": "For if you do so"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s05",
     "source": "The Grass I can mow"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s06",
     "source": "As food for the Cow;"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s07",
     "source": "Madam Cow will give milk"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s08",
     "source": "To the Deer sleek as silk;"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s09",
     "source": "The pain will be borne,"
    },
    {
