     "source": "He will give me his horn,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s11",
     "source": "And I'll dig a clean rill"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s12",
     "source": "For the water to fill;"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s13",
     "source": "Then I'll wash beak and feet"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s14",
     "source": "And the nice *khichrî* eat;"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s15",
     "source": "Though I really don't know"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s16",
     "source": "What the Sparrow can mean,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s17",
     "source": "For I'm sure, as Crows go,"
    },
    {
     "id": "p016.s18",
     "source": "I'm remarkably clean!'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p016"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p017.s01",
     "source": "'With pleasure,' said the Blacksmith, 'if you will light the fire and blow the bellows.'"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p017"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p018.s01",
     "source": "So the Crow began to light the fire, and blow the bellows, but in so doing he fell right in--to--the--very--middle--of--the--*fire*, and was burnt!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p018"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p019.s01",
     "source": "So that was the end of him, and the Sparrow ate all the *khichrî*."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p019"
  }
 ]
